en:
Please do not wash yourself in the sacred waters of the Throne.

&lt;Elementalist Lo'ap holds a prepared caracoli tablet up.&gt;

You place this under your tongue and allow it ample time to dissolve. Once it has dissolved, you will be able to breathe water as if it were air.

ua:
Будь ласка, не омивайся у священних водах Трону.

&lt;Стихієслов Ло'ап підіймає приготовану таблетку караколі.&gt;

Поклади її під язик і дай їй вдосталь часу розчинитися. Щойно вона розчиниться, зможеш дихати водою, наче повітрям.

en:
You have word from the spy mistress?

&lt;The agent looks around to make sure that no one is watching as she puts down her shovel.&gt;

Let me see those plans.

You've done well, young one. I recall a gnome not too long ago completing that trial as well.

Her story was quite the read. But between you and me, gnomes smell like porridge.

&lt;Kronah looks off into the distance, lost in thought for a moment.&gt;

But you are now a bearer of the Bloodshed Contract and one step closer to your final prize.

&lt;Kronah quirks a grin at you and goes back about her business.&gt;

&lt;Pang surveys the area around his farm.&gt;

Well, they're not ALL gone yet, but there's less of them. And they aren't holding their ears quite as high anymore.

I'd guess that they're scared of you, &lt;name&gt;.

ua:
&lt;Панґ оглядає околиці свого господарства.&gt;

Ну, не ВСІ ще зникли, але їх поменшало. І вуха вони вже не тримають так високо.

Гадаю, вони бояться тебе, &lt;name&gt;.

en:
You got the hair?!

&lt;Ms. Xiulan laughs audibly.&gt;

Oh, I wish I could have been there to see the look on his face. Nevertheless, a deal's a deal.

&lt;The Far Seer makes sure to hold the item by the string, carefully avoiding the dead ogre's fist.&gt;

Strange indeed.  I will pass this on to my contacts in the east, near the Mosh'Ogg's main camp.  I have a feeling that they'll be interested in these strange scars.

You have my thanks, &lt;race&gt;.

&lt;Nazgrim listens as you recount the day's events.&gt;

We take the bell... and the Alliance takes Dalaran. That escalated quickly.

War is coming, &lt;name&gt;. Be on your toes.

&lt;Brann looks at the disk as you hold it up.&gt;

I can't tell if there's anything stored there or not! You have to tell me what happened.

&lt;You describe the data retrieval process.&gt;

So it worked? At least we can count on Mimir to be systematic. Can't say that for the rest of these Keepers from what I've been hearing...

You seek training?

&lt;The pandaren studies your physique for several seconds, without speaking.&gt;

Alright.

And you returned victorious, just as I thought! I told Saurfang you'd be fine.

&lt;Hellscream grunts knowingly.&gt;

Perhaps this will show that old dog that he doesn't have all the answers, eh?

&lt;Kalecgos listens to your account of recent events.&gt;

It was wise of Tarecgosa to send you to me, &lt;class&gt;.

Though your vision in the Nexus was almost certainly an elaborate illusion, it would be irresponsible of me not to investigate it.

Now look at that...

&lt;The Rokk takes a sip of the concoction and his face twists into a bizarre mask of pain and delight.&gt;

Sweet A'dal that's good!  A cook with your potential shouldn't be without his proper materials.  Take some of my extra stock and make me proud.

Return triumphant! Valor stick to you like reek of old grease.

&lt;Walkmay pauses, sniffing gingerly.&gt;

That a lot of valor!

&lt;Parvink is covered in bleeding scratches and shredded leaves.&gt;

Hey, not bad! We'll call it a tie. This jungle don't scare me for nothin'.

Maybe we can hunt some more tomorrow?

&lt;Anduin looks like a crumpled doll. He lays as still as a stone, and the only movement comes from the frigid air ruffling his fair, golden hair.&gt;

&lt;You sit quietly for a while, until the cold settles into your bones. The bell is destroyed, but the silence is deafening.&gt;

&lt;Out of the corner of your eye, you see the slightest flicker from the boy's hand. You lean in close. He breathes - but just barely! Anduin is alive!&gt;

That... wasn't what I expected to find out. 

&lt;Lilian clears her throat.&gt;

Family drama aside, whatever the old queen used to be, she'll be a big problem for us when she inevitably shows up on the battlefield.

Brilliant work!

&lt;Tulra tucks the pearls away beneath her armor.&gt;

Now I just need you and Legionnaire Nazgrim to get me safely out of here.  I can handle the studies from there on.

You have done it!

&lt;Goraluk takes the items from your hands, and turns his back for a few moments&gt;

Now, I will touch this Sigil to your hand, and the entrance to the Crucible will open at your touch. Good luck.

ua:
Тобі вдалося!

&lt;Горалук бере предмети з твоїх рук і на мить відвертається.&gt;

Тепер я торкнуся цією Печаткою твоєї руки, і вхід до Горнила відчиниться від твого дотику. Щасти.

en:
Return the tainted sample to Lady Darkglen.
Tainted Sample (1)



WH.ge('icon-list-icon1').appendChild(g_items.createIcon(270562, 0, 1, null, null));

ua:
Поверни осквернений зразок леді Темнодолині.
Осквернений зразок (1)



WH.ge('icon-list-icon1').appendChild(g_items.createIcon(270562, 0, 1, null, null));

en:
&lt;You report your findings to Erunak, who listens distractedly while flipping through the journal you located.&gt;

So... the naga have conscripted sea giants to their cause? This is disturbing.

Adelee's journal confirms my fears. The naga have infiltrated the Abyssal Maw once again, and this time they have a powerful weapon with them: Sharas'dal. Our task is clear.

&lt;Nourman carefully inspects the fangs.&gt;

Checks out. Strange that you got so many. 

Say, you don't look like a venthyr. 

&lt;Nourman shrugs.&gt;

Don't matter to me. You got the fangs, you go inside. Them's the rules.

&lt;Lady Sylvanas Windrunner grimaces in pain.&gt;

This... is not over. Godfrey and his traitorous allies will pay for what they have done as will the remaining Alliance forces occupying Lordaeron.

Our work has only just begun.

We've already lost many brave warriors to this cursed wasteland. I have little interest in sending more untested recruits to the slaughter.

&lt;Nazgrel glares at you sternly through his ragged wolf-mask&gt;

Still, if General Krakork sent you to me, he must have seen something in you. What say you then, &lt;name&gt;? Will you serve your warchief with honor?

Collect 10 Void-Infused Morsels and 6 Glaring Glowcaps outside of the Howling Ridge.
10Void-Infused Morsel (10)
6Glaring Glowcap (6)



