en:
It worked?

&lt;Mordant clears his throat.&gt;

I mean... it worked! Jarl and I are in your debt, &lt;name&gt;. Now the only remaining problem is my friend's taste in furniture, and I'm afraid that won't be solved as easily.

ua:
Спрацювало?

&lt;Мордант прокашлюється.&gt;

Тобто... спрацювало! Ми з Ярлом у боргу перед тобою, {name}. Тепер лишається тільки одна проблема — смак мого друга щодо меблів, і, боюся, її так легко не розв'язати.

en:
&lt;Halford salutes.&gt;

The townsfolk are all back to work? Already? Outstanding, soldier! We'll get this town built back up and fortified in no time. Before long, reinforcements will be ready to join the fight with Lord Fordragon at the Wrathgate.

I'm getting ahead of myself, of course, as there is much left to do here before we can even think about sending you to the aid of Bolvar.

Oh my earring! Why, it matches the one I'm wearing today!

&lt;Tina hooks the earring onto her ear.&gt;

Thank you, &lt;name&gt;!

Greetings, Highlord. What can I help you with?

&lt;You explain what you need to Alard as he looks over the barding.&gt;

I see. I can certainly help you with your upgrading this, but I'll need a few things first.

ua:
Вітаю, Верховний Володарю. Чим можу допомогти?

&lt;Ти пояснюєш Аларду, що потрібно, поки той оглядає обладунок.&gt;

Зрозуміло. Звісно, я можу допомогти тобі це вдосконалити, але спершу мені знадобиться кілька речей.

en:
Teamwork makes the dream work, or so they say. It would appear that the rhyme carries truth to it. Hmmm.

&lt;Eternus pauses for a moment in thought.&gt;

I wonder what other rhymes carry such power. That bears some future experimentation.

