en:
&lt;Brann looks at the disk as you hold it up.&gt;

I can't tell if there's anything stored there or not, lad. You'll have to tell me what happened.

&lt;You describe the data retrieval process.&gt;

So it worked? At least we can count on Keeper Mimir to be systematic.

&lt;Lurielle accepts the cores from you quietly.&gt;

Thank you, &lt;name&gt;.



I promise, my friends, I will do all I can to restore you.

Well? Is he ready to apologize and get back to work? 

&lt;You hand him the satchel of seeds.&gt;

What's this, now?

&lt;Keeshan reads the report.&gt;

DAMN IT! This just got complicated. We've got prisoners of war to rescue before we can blow up the valley. Not to mention the orcs have black dragons on their side.

Are you ready, &lt;name&gt;?

ua:
&lt;Кішан читає донесення.&gt;

От же ж чорт! Усе ускладнилося. Треба врятувати військовополонених, перш ніж підривати долину. Та ще й чорні дракони на боці орків.

Ти $p(готовий:готова), {name}?

en:
So you've brought Timothy's response?

&lt;Kialon pauses a moment to read the letter, then laughs.&gt;

He's got everything under control, he says. Doesn't need help, he says. I could've predicted that!

Some people never change. Look, he even took the time to correct my spelling.

&lt;Kialon lets out a half-hearted sigh.&gt;

I shouldn't have sent the letter. I forgot. The specialist always has the situation under control. Always.

&lt;Kragad frowns as he looks over the goods you found.&gt;

Some of these goods are from Azj-Kahet... We are specifically forbidden from trading with the nerubians in any capacity. We cannot risk any resources falling into the hands of our enemies.

The Councilward must be informed.

&lt;Kil'ruk gives you a strange glance.&gt;

The Klaxxi'va may never accept you fully. Their xenophobic minds are closed to the possibility of a useful &lt;race&gt;.

I, for one, have been proud to fight by your side, &lt;class&gt;. Your presence, and your assistance, do us great honor.

&lt;The King is studying maps of Tanaan Jungle and the surrounding area.&gt;

&lt;name&gt;! The Alliance owes you a great debt for establishing this garrison. Thanks to your bravery and commanding leadership, we've fought this war here on Draenor, instead of amongst our own homes and farmsteads.

It's time now to finish this. Are you ready for the final campaign?

ua:
&lt;Король уважно вивчає карти Танаанських Джунглів і навколишніх земель.&gt;

{name}! Альянс у величезному боргу перед тобою за створення цього гарнізону. Завдяки твоїй хоробрості й уміло виявленому лідерству ми вели цю війну тут, на Дреноре, а не серед власних домівок і хуторів.

Час покінчити з цим. Ти $p(готовий:готова) до завершальної кампанії?

en:
Hmm... interesting.  From what you're saying, it sounds like a fire elemental might have snuck in from Searing Gorge.  Or, the earthquake opened up a crack to the elemental plane...

&lt;Soren laughs uncomfortably.&gt;

Either way, this is bad news.  You should probably report this information to Grelin.

&lt;The raven squawks, and Havi's voice fills your head&gt;

You are indeed mighty, as the trial shows. 

But valor is a different animal - one you think to tame?

ua:
&lt;Крук каркає, і голос Гаві наповнює твою голову&gt;

Ти й справді могутній, як показало випробування.

Але доблесть — це інший звір. Гадаєш, зможеш його приборкати?

en:
Aww, yesss! That's the stuff!

&lt;Noggenfogger pops the cork and dabs some of the potion on his finger.&gt;

Have mercy! WOWZA! I'm going to need some time alone with this stuff!

