en:
As you can see, the Scourge war machine presses onward, yet the armies of the Horde and the Alliance remain divided, making for easy prey. It is for this reason that we must remain united.

&lt;Valus is lost in contemplation for a moment.&gt;

The Argent Crusade has use for a man like you. Perhaps you would be interested in joining our cause? To battle and die at the side of the Ashbringer?

A traitor amongst the tauren?

I've never heard of such a thing. Clan rivalries and warfare are one thing, but killing your own in cold blood.

&lt;Quentin shakes his head in disbelief.&gt;

&lt;T'ara's tusks shift slightly.  Is she smiling?&gt;

You done well.

We gonna rest easy tonight knowin' Jin'do an' Zanzil ain't gonna bind dem powerful beasts against us.

Gah!  These fish are impossible to hit!

&lt;Orako looks at you.&gt;

My wolf got eaten by a fish, and I'm not going back until I find her.

A crystal shard? From a glittering cave? Why does that sound familiar to me?

&lt;She takes the crystal in her hands to examines more closely.&gt;

This can't be! It's the healing crystal I mentioned earlier! We thought it was lost. What a wonder to hold it in my hands...

&lt;She sighs deeply, looking at Munderut.&gt;

I wish it could mend our minds as well as it mends our wounds. We need to get the vault back up and running.

&lt;Gazlowe reads over the schedules quickly, his expression souring.&gt;

Well, good news is Noggenfogger wasn't lyin'.

Bad news is... this is a LOT of names. All gettin' sent to the Kaja'Coast in Zuldazar.

They're a bit rusty, but at least they're intact. Let me explain how these were made...

&lt;Celea begins to describe the method in which the armor was constructed.&gt;

Tedious, yet efficient.

ua:
Трохи заіржавіли, але принаймні цілі. Дай-но розповім, як їх було зроблено...

&lt;Селея починає описувати метод, яким було створено обладунок.&gt;

Марудна робота, але результативна.

en:
&lt;Caladis takes the hilt from you and slowly turns it over in his hands.&gt;

This seems somehow familiar, as though I should know its origins. You say you recovered this in the citadel? Most intriguing.

There are few who possess the ability to make such a blade. Perhaps they can tell us something about your find.

