en:
No need to bring me up to speed... Nespirah has been narrating your adventures as they happened, and Legionnaire Nazgrim filled me in on the rest.

&lt;Duarn closes his eyes and nods.&gt;

Nespirah says that she is quite grateful, and that she has a small surprise ready for the naga.

&lt;Ambo reads through the recovered journal pages.&gt;

There's some good news and there's some bad news. Which do you want first?

Ah hell, why give you a choice? The good news is that if we can get Thel'zan's phylactery, we can destroy him. The bad news is that the phylactery is on a rather large frostwyrm.

A decoder ring? Can't go wrong with the classics I guess.

&lt;Kelsey uses the ring to decode the message.&gt;

This is from Ashvane alright. The date on here is pretty old though. The "patron" she mentions is something they're gonna want to hear about back in Boralus.

ua:
Кільце-дешифратор? Що ж, класика ще нікого не підводила.

&lt;Келсі використовує кільце, щоб розшифрувати повідомлення.&gt;

Це точно від Ешвейн. Хоча дата тут доволі стара. Про "покровителя", якого вона згадує, точно захочуть почути в Боралусі.

en:
Hey, look at how glowy it is!

&lt;Orako looks wistfully off into the distance.&gt;

My wolf loved things that were glowy...

Yeah, I'm sure that you killed all of those bonelashers.  It's obvious since the captain asked for you to turn in proof on that wanted poster.

&lt;Taela gives you a sarcastic look.&gt;

I'll take your word for it.  I'm not certain who I angered to pull this duty, but thanks for your efforts on behalf of the Alliance.  Here's a little something for all of your trouble.

&lt;Chen is actually smiling, despite the villagers' tentative reactions.&gt;

New tastes take time to appreciate. The citrus will rest in their minds--what fruit is it exactly? A sweet lemon? Or a sour melon? It is our nature to seek to understand the unfamiliar.

They'll be back for more--I know it. After all, the Spirit Festival is about celebrating new adventures!

